# SCENARIO: fix_125_heal_log   SEED: 0   CAMERAS: auto   BOTCFG: auto
# Fix #125 (part 1) - no heal is logged "at full HP". Baseline B4 (runs/bl_b4): 60 x "Shymm Dawnsbane:
# HEAL: exura vita (1585/1585)" while hunting Frazzlemaws. Cause: the heal ladder decides on the HP
# BEFORE the cast (hpPct <= 75, or a paralysis cure), but the log printed the HP AFTER it -- so every
# heal that topped the bot up read as a heal at full HP (the DBG snapshot 1.4 s before showed 81 %
# and falling). The ladder was right; the line now reads "HEAL: <words> hp <before>-><after>/<max>
# (decided at N%)[ (paralysis cure)|(emergency)]".
# PRECONDITION: DEBUG MODE, a pinned healer-vocation bot $H sent to a hunt ($HUNT, as in baseline B4):
# castLog lines reach the journal for debug bots. Run: --var H=<name> --var HUNT=<script name>.
# Acceptance over 5 min of hunting: >= 1 heal line in the new format; no heal line whose HP reads full
# in the old format; no ordinary heal (not a paralysis cure) decided above the 75 % threshold.
# Offline replay: python tools/bottest/replay.py <this> runs/bl_b4 -> the old-format check FAILS (60).
@srv audit kinds state,cmd
@srv audit watch $H
@srv audit on expect="enabled=on"
# Batch-4 deploy (2026-11-19): castLog() returns early unless bot.verboseLog, which only a REAL cast
# viewer turns on -- a pinned debug bot alone logs no HEAL line at all (run b4_f125heal: HP dipped to
# 23-69 % and was topped up repeatedly, 0 HEAL lines). The camera is the observer, as in baseline B4.
@cam:$H login
@srv cmd "$H" hunt $HUNT
@srv sleep 300
@srv cmd "$H" status expect="state="
@srv expect src=srv msg~="HEAL: .* hp [0-9]+->[0-9]+/[0-9]+ \(decided at [0-9]+%\)" min=1 within=320
@srv expect-none src=srv msg~="HEAL: [a-z ]+ \(([0-9]+)/\1\)" within=320
@srv expect-none src=srv msg~="HEAL: .*decided at (7[6-9]|[89][0-9]|100)%\)$" within=320
@srv expect-none src=srv msg~="Lua Script Error" within=320
@srv audit watch clear
@srv audit off
@cam:$H logout
